import"./chunk-GAL4ENT6.js";var s="# statefulObservable\r\n\r\nA contest entry built on `@rx-evo/stateful-observable` (from the submodule\r\nsources). Judged by the page tests\r\n(`PAGE_TARGET=stateful-observable npm test`) and the e2e suite\r\n(`E2E_CONTESTER=stateful-observable npm run e2e`). Written by an agent, like\r\nevery entry; the library's maintainer also steered it by hand with general\r\nknowledge of the library, applied to this page ([steering log](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/steering.md)).\r\n\r\nStatus: see [test_report.md](test_report.md), regenerated by `npm run test:report`.\r\nWhat the library covers and what is hand-written: [gaps.md](gaps.md).\r\n\r\n## Extra code\r\n\r\nCode that is not about the page's domain: caches, batching, status mapping,\r\nlifetime, written per entity or as generic helpers. Lines from\r\n[card 06](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/06-boilerplate.md) (Prettier-formatted, non-blank, non-comment), compared with\r\nthe four entries (vanilla-rxjs, ngrx-signal-store, resources,\r\nstateful-observable).\r\n\r\n| Measure | Lines | vs average | vs best | vs worst |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| Extra code (generic + per-entity) | **189** | \u221251% vs average (388) | best | \u2212406 vs worst |\r\n| Whole data layer | **301** | \u221264% vs average (840) | best | \u22121367 vs worst |\r\n| One more batched lookup like `tiers` | **13** | \u221232% vs average (19) | best | \u221217 vs worst |\r\n\r\nThe library's own code is not counted (it is a dependency, like `@ngrx/signals` or Angular's `resource()`).\r\n\r\n## Idea\r\n\r\nEvery piece of data is a stateful observable from `@rx-evo/stateful-observable`.\r\nA server entity addressed by an id (customer, cart, orders, notes, ...) is a\r\nfactory token (`statefulObservableFactory` in an `InjectionToken`, in\r\n`sources/lookups.ts`). A factory gives one shared stream per id, so every reader\r\nof an id reads the same entry: one request, one state. The three batch endpoints\r\n(`tiers`, `ticketCounts`, `prices`) have batch factories\r\n(`statefulObservableBatchFactory`), which collect the ids asked in one tick into\r\ncalls of at most 20.\r\n\r\nState that is keyed by the UI (the customer list's query, the editor's search\r\ntext) is a stateful source owned by its component, with a cache key. Session\r\nstate is `sources/session.ts`: `login` and `logout` write streams, and\r\n`loggedIn$` is derived from them. Every private source is `active: loggedIn$`.\r\n\r\nA section binds independent streams and never joins them. Field components\r\n(`ProductName`, `CustomerTier`, `Kpi`, ...) each project one entity's factory by\r\ntheir own id input and render with `async`. Writes (`utils/action.ts`) are\r\nstreams whose input is a `Subject` of calls, with `exhaustMap`.\r\n\r\n## Good\r\n\r\n- Atomic sources: one source per entity; a counter has one owner and the KPI and\r\n  the open-ticket badge of one customer share its stream (R-J1, R-J7).\r\n- Latest wins by construction: `switchMap` in the stateful inputs, so a late\r\n  answer of customer A cannot reach B (R-C1).\r\n- Session hygiene with no teardown code: `active: loggedIn$` cancels in-flight\r\n  reads and writes at logout and drops the caches (R-S3, R-S4, R-W5).\r\n- Per-section status from the library: `pending$` is the block's `loading`,\r\n  `error$` its `error`; a reload dims the shown data (R-B1, R-C3).\r\n- Polls only while shown: the activity section reloads the entry it shows on a\r\n  timer and stops with the section; the notifications poll is a `timer` in its\r\n  section's loader (R-D2, R-L8).\r\n- Writes with no double submit: `exhaustMap` plus `pending$` (R-W1, R-W2).\r\n\r\n## Bad\r\n\r\nOnly failing requirements and the excess code they cost (spec \xA711). Nothing\r\nfails in the current run (see `test_report.md`); [gaps.md](gaps.md) finds no\r\ngap of the tool.\r\n\r\n- **Excess code for R-G4 and R-C2:** the activity section keeps its list\r\n  through a failed poll by passing the block no error while it shows a list of\r\n  the shown customer. For that, the loader tags each list with its customer\r\n  (one `map` in `ACTIVITY_BY_CUSTOMER`) and the template compares it, a few\r\n  lines.\r\n\r\n## Requirements\r\n\r\n| Requirement | How it is met |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| R-S1 | configuration: `@if (loggedIn())` in the page; `loggedIn$` derived from the write streams |\r\n| R-S2 | configuration: sections subscribe lazily; S4-S10 exist only while the page holds a customer id, panels only while it holds a panel id |\r\n| R-S3 | configuration: `active: loggedIn$` on every private root and factory; the signed-out layout replaces the views |\r\n| R-S4 | built in: `active` drops the cache of every entry, kept ones included; views are recreated and streams are released with their last subscriber |\r\n| R-S5 | helper (`sources/session.ts`, `LAST_TAB`): a root signal the tabs card reads on mount and writes on every tab change; customer and panel are component state and reset |\r\n| R-D1 | configuration: factories, a stateful source per keyed section (key as input, factory entry as loader), one `pipeValue` per view input |\r\n| R-D2 | helper: `timer(0, 30_000)` in the notifications section's loader; a 20 s `timer` in the activity section that reloads the shown entry |\r\n| R-B1 | built in: `app-stateful-block` takes `[stream]`; its `pending$` and `error$` drive the block |\r\n| R-J1 | configuration: every other-service value is a field component over a projection of the entity's factory; nothing unresolved shows as an empty space |\r\n| R-J2 | built in: one id per call, so the answer holds the item of that id and nothing else |\r\n| R-J3 | configuration: batch factories (`tiers`, `ticketCounts`, `prices`) send at most 20 ids per call |\r\n| R-J4 | configuration: cart and hits read `currentPrice`; order lines read the `unitPrice` of the order |\r\n| R-J5 | helper (`linkedTicketOf` in `vm/vm.ts`) over the `ticketsByOrder` stream of the order |\r\n| R-J6 | not in the data layer: the shared views write the sentences from kind, refs and the name field component |\r\n| R-J7 | built in: counters come from the `orderStats`, `ticketCounts`, `tiers` and `customer` factories only |\r\n| R-C1 | built in: `switchMap` in the stateful inputs; the next key's loader replaces the previous one |\r\n| R-C2 | built in: `pending$` stays on while a source holds another key's data, so the block dims until the current key arrives |\r\n| R-W1 | configuration: `result.pending$` of the write stream goes into the view's `ActionState` |\r\n| R-W2 | configuration: `mapOperator: exhaustMap`, and the pending state disables the control |\r\n| R-W3 | helper (`utils/action.ts` and the owning component): `reload()` of the affected factory entries in the write's `tap` |\r\n| R-W5 | built in: `active: loggedIn$` on the write stream drops a late answer |\r\n| R-W6 | not in the data layer: the shared order view offers Create return |\r\n| R-W7 | not used: no optimistic display |\r\n| R-B2 | built in: `app-stateful-block` replaces the spinner block in every section |\r\n| R-E1 | built in: `error$` of the source takes the block's error branch; a section with data keeps it |\r\n| R-E2 | built in: a new key's loader runs as soon as its input changes |\r\n| R-E3 | built in: `result.error$` of the write goes into the control's `ActionState` |\r\n| R-G1 | configuration: the block's `[error]` is set while the main source's `error$` is set |\r\n| R-G2 | configuration: `[error]` names the failed source (`Couldn't load <source>`) |\r\n| R-G3 | configuration: each field stream fails on its own; the order panel's ticket box reads its own `error$` |\r\n| R-G4 | helper: activity: the template shows the error only while there is no list of the shown customer; notifications: the loader drops a failed poll after the first answer (`catchError(() => EMPTY)`) |\r\n| R-G5 | configuration: `(retry)` calls `reload()` of the failed source only |\r\n| R-G6 | configuration: field templates read their own `error$`; a failed price or stock disables the hit's Add, and a failed `orderStats` empties its count |\r\n| R-C3 | built in: a reload keeps the content and dims it through `pending$` |\r\n| R-C4 | built in: a superseded read is cancelled by the library's default factory |\r\n| R-W8 | configuration: the write stream is owned by the page and is not tied to a section, so a navigation does not stop it |\r\n| R-W9 | built in: `result.error$` goes into the control's `ActionState`; the write's `tap` (the refreshes) runs only on success |\r\n| R-W10 | configuration: the write's `tap` reloads the factory entries of exactly the affected keys, for `updateOrder` the stock of the skus before and after the change (C16) |\r\n| R-L1 | configuration: `active: loggedIn$` on every source; polls stop with the session |\r\n| R-L2 | built in: a section's stream starts with its subscriber, so a section not shown sends nothing |\r\n| R-L3 | built in: one entry per key in the factory |\r\n| R-L4 | configuration: a `debounce` in the stateful input of the customer list and the order editor's search |\r\n| R-L11 | configuration: the sentence name fields are their own projections, requested by the notification's customer id |\r\n| R-L9 | configuration: the editor's price lookups use `statefulObservableBatchFactory`, one batch per search (`sources/lookups.ts`) |\r\n| R-L10 | built in: `project(input$)` resolves to the same stream as `get(value)`, so one entry, one request |\r\n| R-L5 | built in: a settled value stays cached while a session lasts |\r\n| R-L6 | configuration: the public factories (`productName`, `currentPrice`, `stockBySku`, product search) are not `active: loggedIn$` |\r\n| R-L7 | helper: a write's `tap` reloads the entries the write changed |\r\n| R-L8 | helper: each poll lives in its section and stops with it; the activity poll reloads only the shown customer's entry (C15) |\r\n| R-P1 | built in: independent streams start in parallel, and each section renders when its own data arrives |\r\n| R-P2 | configuration: the in-flight orders list and each row's shipment are separate sources |\r\n| R-P3 | configuration: the order's line names are field components that follow the order |\r\n| R-P4 | built in: a projection starts when its key arrives |\r\n| R-P5 | configuration: the input filters `null` out, so no request starts while a key is missing |\r\n| R-P6 | configuration: each cart line's price and name are separate field components over their own factories |\r\n\r\n## Tradeoffs\r\n\r\nEight criteria, the same in every entry's README. Each is compared across the entries in [docs/contest/results](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/criteria.md); the numbers below come from there (line counts: card [06](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/06-boilerplate.md), Prettier-formatted, non-blank, non-comment).\r\n\r\n- **Eager or lazy start.** Lazy. A stateful stream starts with its first subscriber, and `active` gates it on the session (`sources/lookups.ts`, `sources/session.ts`). Gives: a section that is not shown sends nothing. Costs: stream identity has to be understood to know when a request starts.\r\n- **One request per key, and how long a value lives.** A factory gives one entry per key; the entry is released with its last subscriber, and `active: loggedIn$` drops every entry at logout. A settled value is kept after its last subscriber leaves, up to `cacheSize` (default 42; 200 or 500 where set). Gives: one request per key, with cleanup done by the library. Costs: the bound is per factory, set by hand where the default does not fit.\r\n- **Cancelling a superseded read.** Built in: the library cancels a superseded read with the default factory. The six `refCount: false` lookups keep their read running on purpose, to keep the value. Gives: no code in the entry. Costs: the behaviour is the library's, not this entry's to change.\r\n- **Batching.** Built in: `statefulObservableBatchFactory` collects the ids of one tick into calls of at most 20 (`sources/lookups.ts`). Gives: batching by configuration. Costs: the batch path is the library's, and nothing on it fails in the current run.\r\n- **Keeping data on error or reload.** `pending$` and `error$` are per stream; a reload dims the shown data, and on a key switch the last value stays under the spinner (R-C2). The block shows the error or the content. Gives: stale content is shown dimmed, not blanked. Costs: a view that keeps its value through an error overrides the block's error itself (the activity section, with its customer tag).\r\n- **Boilerplate to add one value.** One more batched lookup like `tiers` costs 13 lines in 2 files, the factory token being configuration. The data layer is 301 lines: 48 generic, 141 per entity (17 lookups), 112 domain. Costs: each field is its own `app-stateful-block` with `[stream]` and one `async` read of `value$`.\r\n- **Where state lives.** Session and caches at root; the selected customer and open panel in components, passed down as inputs and up as events; the last tab in a root token (`LAST_TAB`). Gives: component state is local and explicit. Costs: the selection resets on navigation.\r\n- **Dependency on a library.** `@rx-evo/stateful-observable`. Gives: the library's own cache policy. Costs: the entry was steered by the library's maintainer, so it is not an independent judge of the library; stated, not scored.\r\n\r\n## Try it\r\n\r\n1. Open `?seed=1&latency=slow`, sign in, select a customer, then quickly\r\n   another: the main column dims under the spinner and then shows the new\r\n   customer; the list rows fill in from their own requests.\r\n2. Open the Cart of a customer with a long cart: each name arrives on its own, each\r\n   price and line total in its own cell.\r\n3. Open an order of a ticket, edit items, add a product, save and reply: the\r\n   order, the cart row, the KPIs and the list badge refresh from the reloaded\r\n   entries.\r\n4. Log out while a slow request is pending, then log in again: nothing of the\r\n   previous session shows, and the late answer is dropped.\r\n5. Fail a source with the error toggles of the fake API: its section shows the\r\n   error with Retry in place of the view; Retry asks only that source again.\r\n";export{s as default};
